        <h2>2. Herman Miller Aeron Size C — Best Mesh Chair for Tall Users Who Run Warm</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Tall users 6'0"–6'3" who prioritize breathability and run hot.<br/>
        <strong>Price:</strong> ~$1,600–$1,800 new; ~$600–$1,000 certified refurbished<br/>
        <strong>Key specs:</strong> 16"–20.5" seat height, ~18.5" fixed seat depth, ~20.5" seat width, 350 lb weight capacity, Pellicle mesh seat and back</p>

        <p>The Aeron Size C is sized for taller frames — Size C is the large version of the <a href="/chairs/herman-miller-aeron/size-guide/">three Aeron sizes (A, B, C)</a> and is intended for users up to about 6'3". Its Pellicle mesh construction (mesh seat and back with no foam layer) provides class-leading breathability that matters for users spending 6+ hours in a chair in a non-air-conditioned environment.</p>

        <p>The dimensional constraints to understand: the 20.5" seat height ceiling is adequate for most users through 6'3" but starts to strain above that. The fixed ~18.5" seat depth is reasonable for users at 6'0"–6'3" with average proportions, but it is not adjustable — users with longer femurs may find it short. The 350 lb weight capacity is the lowest in this guide and is a relevant constraint for heavier tall users.</p>

        <p>The Aeron's PostureFit SL lumbar system (a two-pad mechanism supporting both the sacrum and lumbar) is frequently cited in ergonomics communities as one of the strongest lower-back support implementations available. For tall users whose primary concern is back support and heat management rather than maximum seat height, the Size C is a strong option.</p>

