        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Tall users 6'0"–6'2" who want a recognizable brand at a budget price point with 400 lb capacity.<br/>
        <strong>Price:</strong> ~$350–$450<br/>
        <strong>Key specs:</strong> ~19"–21" seat height, ~19" fixed seat depth, ~22" seat width, 400 lb weight capacity, foam padded seat</p>

        <p>The La-Z-Boy Trafford is the most common budget big-and-tall recommendation in retail channels and has a wide seat at ~22" — one of the widest available in this price range. Its 400 lb weight capacity and ~21" seat height ceiling cover the dimensional and structural needs of most users at 6'0"–6'2".</p>

        <p>The main limitation is fixed seat depth (~19") and a foam-padded seat construction. The fixed depth is borderline adequate at 6'2" and insufficient for users with longer femurs above that. The foam retains more heat than mesh alternatives and will compress over time, reducing effective seat depth. Community reports suggest the cushion noticeably softens after 12–18 months of daily use.</p>

        <p>For tall users at 6'0"–6'2" who need 400 lb capacity and cannot justify premium chair pricing, the Trafford is a reasonable practical choice. For users above 6'2" or those planning 5+ years of daily use, the <a href="/refurbished-steelcase-leap-tall-people/" class="link-internal">refurbished Steelcase Leap V2</a> is a better investment at a similar price point.</p>

